Keep water's DllMain out of the DLL exports

water records the module it is linked into from DllMain, and exports
DllMain to keep it. Built as shared libraries, libcarla_native-plugin,
libcarla_host-plugin and libcarla_standalone2 therefore export DllMain,
and a DLL linked to one of them without a DllMain of its own resolves
its own to that import: its startup then calls Carla's DllMain with its
own module handle, and carla_get_library_filename() and
carla_get_library_folder() name that DLL instead of Carla's. LMMS's
carlabase is such a DLL. The C runtime's startup code calls DllMain
within the same DLL, so it needs no export.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/source/modules/water/water.cpp b/source/modules/water/water.cpp
--- a/source/modules/water/water.cpp
+++ b/source/modules/water/water.cpp
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ HINSTANCE getCurrentModuleInstanceHandle() noexcept
 }
 
